time command



Example:
time ls

Output : 
real    0m0.003s
user    0m0.001s
sys     0m0.002s

What they mean
real → Actual elapsed time from start to finish.
user → CPU time spent executing your program's code in user space.
sys → CPU time spent in the kernel on behalf of the program.


time → measures command execution time
real  → wall-clock time
user  → user-space CPU time
sys   → kernel CPU time
